WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.500
- So I'm a mom of
(crowd applauses)

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.510
two wonderful girls.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:04.640
Maybe I'm a little biased.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.810
But listen, it's a job that has proven

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.369
to be one of the most
difficult jobs I've ever had.

00:00:09.369 --> 00:00:12.140
But the most rewarding.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:13.920
And I wanna keep moms connected

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:15.880
and supported and heard.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.150
Well, giving them a break
when they need it the most.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.740
So when I heard the story of the mom

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.720
behind this viral picture,

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.890
and I do mean it went everywhere.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:30.290
I knew that I wanted to get to know her.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:33.663
And this is our very first moms timeout.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.610
(happy music)

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:38.500
- I'm Jana Coombs.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.820
I'm a mom to four beautiful kiddos ages

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.570
nine, seven, five,

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:44.220
and eight months old.
(giggling)

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.670
I live in Sharpsburg Georgia.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.690
My husband, Luke, is
an essential employee.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:50.290
He's went to work throughout
the entire pandemic.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:52.493
So we've been busy to say the least.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.348
I like live in the kitchen.

00:00:55.348 --> 00:00:57.130
Between four kids,
(happy music continues)

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:58.380
living in the kitchen.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.360
Trying to explain
(soft music)

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.610
to kids what COVID is

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:05.000
was kind of hard because
they don't understand

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.150
the magnitude of the situation.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:09.340
And for them to not be able to go out

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.450
and see their friends
was very challenging.

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:12.283
They didn't understand
(soft music continues)

00:01:12.283 --> 00:01:14.960
why school wasn't starting.
The most difficult time

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.810
throughout this pandemic
has definitely been

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.580
the first day of As Rose
Kindergarten, virtual learning.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:23.210
And within the first 45 minutes

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:24.760
is when all of this took place.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.850
He just bowed his head down
and his tears were just rolling

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.230
down his face and he
had his shirt pulled up

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:32.559
and he just was so overwhelmed.

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.680
Not just broke my heart

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.120
because for a child to sit there

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.400
and cry, it just shatters your world.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.240
Cause as moms, we want
to take that pain away.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.190
We want them to be excited for school.

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:45.603
We want them to learn with enthusiasm.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.980
I was very hesitant to post
this photo on Facebook,

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:51.810
but I knew that I wanted
other moms to see.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.840
And that photo quickly went viral.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.085
We've had thousands of
shares, millions of comments

00:01:57.085 --> 00:01:59.970
and it made headline news
all around the world.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:04.850
So I knew that was really
resonating with a lot of families.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.470
I know that I'm only one voice,

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:07.910
but I hope by sharing my story

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:11.460
that it helps other
mothers not feel alone.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:12.970
That we're just trying to keep it together

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:14.821
one day at a time for our kids.

00:02:14.821 --> 00:02:16.320
(indistinct)

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.496
- Bye,

00:02:17.496 --> 00:02:18.329
bye.

00:02:19.616 --> 00:02:20.449
(crowd applauds)

00:02:20.449 --> 00:02:22.397
- Welcome Jana for our very

00:02:22.397 --> 00:02:25.671
- [Jana] Hi.
- first moms time out.

00:02:25.671 --> 00:02:28.960
(crowd applauds)
- Hi, so excited to be here.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:29.800
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:33.090
I am, thank you for coming on our show

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:36.630
because I can imagine
everybody wants to talk

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:37.980
to you about this

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:42.100
and the way that you described
your situation with Ezra,

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.510
you know, about how you
want to take the pain away.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:45.370
As a parent,
- Yeah.

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:46.910
- when they're suffering.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.440
I just really was in awe of

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:51.710
how well you told your story.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:52.543
And I think that's
- [Jana] Thank you so much.

00:02:52.543 --> 00:02:54.760
- [Drew] why it resonated
with so many people.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.563
How are you in Ezra now?

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:58.370
- We're doing good.

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:01.290
Our County allowed face to
face learning to start again.

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:02.730
So he was very excited

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:05.920
and seeing my kids happy,
just makes me happy.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:09.750
- Okay, so Ezra is back in school, right?

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:10.740
- Yes.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.120
- Okay.
- Yes, he is.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.633
- How is that going?

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:15.460
- It's going great.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:16.820
He is so excited to be back

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.440
with his teachers and his friends.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.580
And he just said," Mom,
it feels normal again."

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.970
So just having that normalcy happen again,

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.260
just puts a smile on my face

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.460
because that's all I want
for my kids right now.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:29.270
- And why do you think if you could guess

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:32.843
why this picture made such
an impact with people?

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:35.821
- I think that it's just
reality for so many,

00:03:35.821 --> 00:03:38.140
like you said, it's not just Ezra

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:39.600
or myself going through this.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:41.660
It's all of our kids, many ages.

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:42.970
It's not just kindergartners.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:43.803
It's first, second, third,

00:03:43.803 --> 00:03:45.980
and middle school and high school.

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:47.310
So we're all in this together.

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:49.370
Just taking it one day at a time.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.470
- I also wanna mention that your husband

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:54.400
is an essential worker and
- He is.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.910
- that's another thing

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:59.260
that's a really important
narrative this year.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:01.713
How do you manage all of this together?

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.170
- So it leaves a little bit of a less time

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.230
but he's been really
supportive and gives me

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.620
lots of breaks as well.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:11.004
But with him being gone,
I think just adding

00:04:11.004 --> 00:04:13.710
being a teacher in two, three kids

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.860
and having an infant has been really hard,

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:19.798
sometimes it's next to impossible (laughs)

00:04:19.798 --> 00:04:21.460
(sighs)
- [Drew] I can only imagine.

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:24.043
(upbeat music)

